\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  See! In yonder manger low,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Born for us on earth below,
\par  See! The tender Lamb appears
\par  Promised from eternal years.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par \i0 Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem,
\par  'Christ is born in Bethlehem!'
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Lo! Within a manger lies
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  He who built the starry skies,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0   He who, throned in height sublime,
\par  Sits  amid the cherubim
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par \i0 Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem,
\par  'Christ is born in Bethlehem!'
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Say, ye  holy shepherds, say,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  What your joyful news today;
\par  Wherefore have ye left your sheep
\par  On the lonely mountain steep?
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par \i0 Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem,
\par  'Christ is born in Bethlehem!'
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  ' As we watched at dead of night,
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  Lo! We saw a wondrous light:
\par  Angels, singing peace on earth,
\par  Told us of the Saviour's birth.'
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par \i0 Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem,
\par  'Christ is born in Bethlehem!'
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Sacred Infant, all Divine,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  What a tender love was thine,
\par  Thus to come from highest bliss
\par \pard       Down to such a world as this!
\par 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0\i 
\par \i0 Hail, thou ever-blessed morn!
\par Hail, redemption's happy dawn!
\par Sing through all Jerusalem,
\par  'Christ is born in Bethlehem!'\cf1\ul\b\f1 
\par }

